\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Main result pattern and controls. (A) On MB140 fold 0 under the strict prefix-only protocol, decoupled-oracle workflow conditioning improves MAE by 0.85 min over no-token. (B) The same decoupled architecture gives a smaller but positive cross-center gain from Bern to Strasbourg. (C) Cholec80 is the low-variability contrast case: the centered-window teacher-forced prefix penalty does not reproduce under the strict protocol. (D) Shuffling workflow tokens destroys the gain, supporting the interpretation that the token carries workflow meaning rather than merely adding parameter capacity.}}{8}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:main-result-pattern}{{2}{8}{Main result pattern and controls. (A) On MB140 fold 0 under the strict prefix-only protocol, decoupled-oracle workflow conditioning improves MAE by 0.85 min over no-token. (B) The same decoupled architecture gives a smaller but positive cross-center gain from Bern to Strasbourg. (C) Cholec80 is the low-variability contrast case: the centered-window teacher-forced prefix penalty does not reproduce under the strict protocol. (D) Shuffling workflow tokens destroys the gain, supporting the interpretation that the token carries workflow meaning rather than merely adding parameter capacity}{figure.caption.4}{}}
